title: "What Is to Be Done?"
card-image: img/cards/neorevisionism.svg?v=2
subtitle: The party's own programme for the Soviet economy.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik' and (neorevisionism_timer <= 0 and bol_regime = 1 and dix >= 44 and program_adopted = 0)
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1; Q.neorevisionism_timer = 2;
Q.nr_rb = Math.floor(Q.rel_bol);
!}

The Bolshevik economic policy, War Communism, takes grain from the peasants by force. The factories are idle, the cities are starving and the party's economists have drafted an alternative: end requisitioning, allow free trade in grain, give the unions independence and restore a regulated market.

What it can win: if, in the summer of 1919, the programme is published and relations with the Bolsheviks are at least 43 (now [+ nr_rb +]), Lenin will try it, "the NEP before the NEP". The programme, relations of 43 and soviet democracy of 45 are also what the demand for free soviet elections at the Eighth Congress of Soviets, in December 1920, needs.

- @adopt: Adopt the programme and publish it. (1 resource)
- @study: Study it more before adopting.
- @easy_discard

@adopt
subtitle: Workers, peasants, railwaymen and the middle classes +; relations with the Bolsheviks -2, repression +2.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no resources.
on-arrival: {!
RO.pay(Q, 1);
Q.program_adopted = 1;
Q.program_year = Q.year;
Q.program_dix = Q.dix;
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, peasants: 3, railway: 3, middle: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 3, -4);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 1, -2);
RO.add(Q, {repression: 2, bread: 2, rel_bol: -2});
!}

The programme was published as an open letter to the Central Executive Committee. It said what everyone at the front and in the villages already thinks. The Bolsheviks have not answered, and the Cheka has noticed who signed it.

@study
on-arrival: {!
Q.neorevisionism_timer = 1;
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 1, 0);
!}

Our economists will write it up properly. It may be ready next turn.
